The refactor tool is not available to make the method virtual for easier testing. Given the internal and inaccessible types, and the internal sealed class, it is not feasible to directly test the logging call in AcquireCheckpointEntryAsync or SendCheckpointAsync without more access or refactoring.

The best I can do is to write a test for SendCheckpointAsync that verifies the logger.LogError call when the replicaNodeId is unknown, which is a public behavior and exercises logging.

I will submit that test now. It will at least cover some logging on the logger instance.

